  "description": "ThinkGeo.Gpu renders ThinkGeo maps on the GPU from a style.json document: vector and raster tiles, a perspective camera, terrain, extrusions and label placement. It carries no UI stack, so a host supplies presentation and input - the ThinkGeo UI packages do that for you, and a server or headless application can drive it directly through software rasterization.",
